From 63e3bb41bf01f92e2498285ccc6dc498b31cd672 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ondrej Jirman <megi@xff.cz>
Date: Sun, 2 Aug 2026 19:16:56 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] media: hm5065: Ask to be probed again if the camera is silent

Moving the identification into probe made the driver depend on the
camera answering at probe time, and on this board it does not: during
boot it says nothing at all, however long it is given and however
many times it is power cycled, while the same driver bound by hand
once the machine is up works every time. The driver this replaced
never noticed, because it only touched the camera when the device was
opened, long after boot.

Return -EPROBE_DEFER instead of failing, so a camera that is merely
late still ends up working, and keep failing for a wrong chip id.

Signed-off-by: Ondrej Jirman <megi@xff.cz>
---
 drivers/media/i2c/hm5065.c | 16 +++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/i2c/hm5065.c b/drivers/media/i2c/hm5065.c
index 9a8e8c53dd9a..f751476eb372 100644
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/hm5065.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/hm5065.c
@@ -2351,8 +2351,22 @@ static int hm5065_probe(struct i2c_client *client)
 		goto entity_cleanup;
 
 	ret = hm5065_identify(sensor);
-	if (ret)
+	if (ret) {
+		/*
+		 * The camera is not reachable this early during boot on
+		 * some boards - it answers nothing at all, however long it
+		 * is given and however many times it is power cycled, and
+		 * only starts talking once the machine is up. Before the
+		 * identification moved into probe nothing noticed, because
+		 * the first transfer happened when the device was opened.
+		 * Ask to be probed again rather than losing the camera for
+		 * the rest of the boot.
+		 */
+		if (ret != -ENODEV)
+			ret = -EPROBE_DEFER;
+
 		goto power_off;
+	}
 
 	ret = hm5065_init_controls(sensor);
 	if (ret)
-- 
